<div class="bg-zinc-950 text-zinc-100" phx-no-curly-interpolation>
  <.marketing_nav current_user={@current_user} current={:docs} />

  <section class="py-12 sm:py-16">
    <.docs_layout
      current="connect-nono"
      updated="September 9, 2026"
      evidence="Tested with nono 0.75.0 on macOS on September 7, 2026."
      toc={[
        {"connect", "Connect nono"},
        {"limits-and-risks", "Limits & risks"},
        {"rotation", "Rotate the key"}
      ]}
    >
      <.docs_header current="connect-nono">
        <:dek>
          Run a local CLI agent under nono's operating-system sandbox and extend that control to
          infrastructure and third-party tools with emisar.
        </:dek>
      </.docs_header>

      <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
        nono limits the files, environment variables, commands, and network destinations available
        to a local process. emisar separately limits the infrastructure actions that process can
        request.
      </p>

      <.docs_prerequisites>
        <:item>
          A macOS or Linux computer and Codex available in nono's <.link
            href="https://registry.nono.sh"
            class="text-brand-400 hover:text-brand-300"
          >profile registry</.link>.
        </:item>
        <:item>
          Codex installed and signed in. Keep its provider credentials in the location the nono
          profile expects; do not copy them into the project.
        </:item>
        <:item>
          An emisar account with permission to connect an agent and at least one runner online.
          Complete the
          <.link
            navigate={~p"/docs/quickstart"}
            class="text-brand-400 hover:text-brand-300"
          >quickstart</.link>
          first if you do not have a runner yet.
        </:item>
      </.docs_prerequisites>

      <.docs_sandbox_connection
        name="nono"
        connect_href={~p"/app/agents/connect"}
        audit_href={~p"/app/audit"}
        policy_href={~p"/docs/policies-and-approvals"}
      />

      <.docs_h2 id="limits-and-risks">Limits &amp; risks</.docs_h2>
      <ul class="mt-5 list-disc space-y-3 pl-6 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
        <li>
          nono enforces the profile you run. It does not hide files or block network destinations
          that the profile itself allows, including files in the working directory.
        </li>
        <li>
          The agent can read its own MCP configuration, including its emisar key. emisar policy,
          approvals, runner scope, and audit still apply to every request.
        </li>
        <li>
          Review every file, command, environment, or network permission you add to the profile.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <.docs_h2 id="rotation">Rotate the key</.docs_h2>
      <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
        Automatic key rotation is unavailable in the strict macOS profile used for qualification.
        Rotate the key from <a
          href={~p"/app/agents"}
          class="font-medium text-brand-300 underline decoration-brand-500/30 underline-offset-4 hover:text-brand-200"
        >AI agents</a>, replace it in the private Codex configuration, and start a fresh nono
        session. Do not grant the sandbox an entire credential directory just to enable automatic
        rotation.
      </p>
    </.docs_layout>
  </section>

  <.marketing_footer />
</div>
